 * Chartography (w/tools): 78.9\nL31:   * BabyVision (w/tools): 89.6\nL32:   * ZeroBench-main (w/tools): 49.0\nL33: * Tested only on the pure-text subset of the HLE benchmark set.\nL34: \nL35: API changes\nL36: \nL37: DeepSeek V4.1 Flash is now available on the DeepSeek API with native multimodal support. Change the model name to `deepseek-flash` to call the latest V4.1 Flash model. The previous-generation models V4 Flash and V4 Flash Vision Exp have been retired; for compatibility, the model names `deepseek-v4-flash` and `deepseek-v4-flash-vision-exp` are temporarily routed to V4.1 Flash.\nL38: In response to user demand, we have decided to continue providing API services for DeepSeek V4 Pro after September 14, 2026, with the billing method remaining unchanged. We will provide further notice should there be any changes. Thank you for your understanding and support!\nL39: \nL40: API pricing adjustment\nL41: \nL42: With the release of DeepSeek-V4.1-Flash, API prices have been reduced accordingly. For details, please refer to cite4†Models & Pricing .\nL43: \nL44: For more details, please refer to cite5†this documentation .\nL45: \nL46: * * *\nL47: ## Date: 2026-08-21cite6†​ L48: ### DeepSeek-V4-Flash-Vision-Exp Releasecite7†​ L49: \nL50: Today, the new multimodal vision understanding model DeepSeek-V4-Flash-Vision-Exp is now available on the DeepSeek API platform. This is an experimental model that can be accessed by setting `model='deepseek-v4-flash-vision-exp'`.\nL51: \nL52:   * Terminal Bench 2.1: 83.9\nL53:   * NL2Repo: 57.7\nL54:   * DeepSWE: 59.3\nL55:   * DSBench-Hard: 63.6\nL56:   * AutomationBench (Public): 25.7\nL57:   * ApexBench (Pass@1): 36.5\nL58:   * Agents' Last Exam: 27.3\nL59:   * Chartography: 64.3\nL60:   * ZeroBench (Pass@5): 35.0\nL61: * For the Code Agent text tasks in the public benchmark sets, the DeepSeek family models were tested using the DeepSeek Harness minimal mode as the framework, with the max effort level, topp=0.95, and temperature=1.0; in the ApexBench and Agents' Last Exam evaluations, the text model DeepSeek-V4-Flash ignores the multimodal elements within them.\nL62: \nL63: In terms of pure-text capabilities (agent, reasoning, world knowledge, etc.), DeepSeek-V4-Flash-Vision-Exp is on par with the official DeepSeek-V4-Flash.\nL64: On agent benchmarks that require visual understanding, DeepSeek-V4-Flash-Vision-Exp delivers a significant leap over DeepSeek-V4-Flash, bringing its multimodal agent capabilities close to Opus-4.8.\nL65: \nL66: For usage details, please refer to the cite8†Vision guide .\nL67: \nL68: * * *\nL69: ## Date: 2026-08-13cite9†​ L70: ### DeepSeek-V4-Pro Updatecite10†​ L71: \nL72: The GA release of DeepSeek-V4-Pro has been rolled out on the APP, Web, and API. The API calling method remains unchanged — simply set the model name to `deepseek-v4-pro` to use the latest version.\nL73: \nL74: Significantly enhanced Agent capabilities\nL75: \nL76: The GA version of DeepSeek V4 Pro greatly enhances agent capabilities, with particularly significant performance improvements in production environments.\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nNew Released - Overview - Z.AI DEVELOPER DOCUMENT (https://docs.z.ai/release-notes/new-released)\nciteturn31836view7 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: today; Content type: text/html; Source: open({\"ref_id\":\"https://docs.z.ai/release-notes/new-released\",\"lineno\":70}); Total lines: 165\nL57:   * Designed for long-horizon tasks, GLM-5.1 can work independently for up to 8 hours in a single run, enabling a full loop from planning and execution to iterative refinement and final delivery.\nL58:   * It demonstrates stronger engineering intelligence across autonomous planning, sustained execution, bug fixing, and strategy iteration, while achieving comprehensive capability alignment with Claude Opus 4.6. Built with multi-turn SFT, RL, and a process-quality evaluation framework, GLM-5.1 further improves stability, consistency, and tool use over extended tasks. Learn more in our cite17†documentation .*\nL59: cite18†​ L60: \nL61: [Button: 2026-02-12]\nL62: \nL63: GLM-5\nL64:   * Designed for complex system engineering and long-range Agent tasks, GLM-5 shifts the paradigm from coding to engineering, demonstrating strong deep-reasoning performance in backend architecture, complex algorithms, and stubborn bug fixing.\nL65:   * It directly benchmarks against Claude Opus 4.5 in code-logic density and systems-engineering capability, and integrates DeepSeek Sparse Attention for higher token efficiency while preserving long-context quality.Learn more in our cite19†documentation .*\nL66: \nL67: cite20†​ L68: [Button: 2026-02-03]\nL69: \nL70: GLM-OCR\nL71:   * We’ve launched GLM-OCR, a compact and high-performance optical character recognition model powered by the self-developed CogViT and GLM-0.5B encoder-decoder architecture, enabling efficient cross-modal alignment through its dedicated connection layer.\nL72:   * The update leverages CLIP pre-training on billions of image-text pairs to deliver robust visual semantic understanding and key token extraction capabilities, while maintaining a lightweight design for fast inference. Learn more in our cite21†documentation .*\nL73: cite22†​ L74: \nL75: [Button: 2026-01-19]\nL76: \nL77: GLM-4.7-Flash\nL78:   * We’ve launched GLM-4.7-Flash, a lightweight and efficient model designed as the free-tier version of GLM-4.7, delivering strong performance across coding, reasoning, and generative tasks with low latency and high throughput.\nL79:   * The update brings competitive coding capabilities at its scale, offering best-in-class general abilities in writing, translation, long-form content, role play, and aesthetic outputs for high-frequency and real-time use cases. Learn more in our cite23†documentation .*\nL80: \nL81: cite24†​ L82: [Button: 2026-01-14]\nL83: \nL84: GLM-Image\nL85:   * We’ve launched GLM-Image, a state-of-the-art image generation model built on a multimodal architecture and fully trained on domestic chips, combining autoregressive semantic understanding with diffusion-based decoding to deliver high-quality, controllable visual generation.\nL86:   * The update significantly enhances performance in knowledge-intensive scenarios, with more stable and accurate text rendering inside images, making GLM-Image especially well suited for commercial design, educational illustrations, and content-rich visual applications.Learn more in our cite25†documentation .*\nL87: cite26†​ L88: \nL89: [Button: 2025-12-22]\nL90: \nL91: GLM-4.7\nL92:   * We’ve released GLM-4.7, our foundation model with significant improvements in coding, reasoning, and agentic capabilities. It delivers more reliable code generation, stronger long-context understanding, and improved end-to-end task execution across real-world development workflows.\nL93:   * The update brings open-source SOTA performance on major coding and reasoning benchmarks, enhanced agentic coding for goal-driven, multi-step tasks, and improved front-end and document generation quality. Learn more in our cite23†documentation .*\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nInternal Error ()\nciteturn31836view8 [wordlim: 200] Source: open({\"ref_id\":\"https://www.zhipuai.cn/zh/research\",\"lineno\":null}); Total lines: 1\n"
